                <pb facs="1042" n="946" xml:id="pg946"/>

                <head>No. 618.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Sickles to Mr. Fish</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 16,
                        1873</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Layard informs me he has received instructions from his government concerning
                    seventeen British subjects among the crew of the Vir-ginius executed, and seven
                    more under sentence of death, the latter all minors. Of the seventeen dead, six
                    were executed immediately on the arrival of the Virginius in port. A British
                    frigate is ordered to Santiago.</p>
                <closer><signed>SICKLES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
